Note for anyone redistributing or building on this software: it deliberately
contains a component that misbehaves. src/seller/dishonest.ts is a mock seller
that accepts payment and returns fabricated values. It exists so the delivery
verification can be seen catching it, and it is labelled as a mock in its own
source header, at startup, and in the README. Do not deploy it as a real service.

This software depends on Apache-2.0 licensed components from the x402 Foundation
(@x402/core, @x402/hedera) and the Hiero project (@hiero-ledger/sdk).

Payments in this demo settle through Blocky402, an open x402 facilitator
operated by BlockyDevs (https://blocky402.com, https://github.com/blockydevs).
Blocky402 is a separate service, not included in or distributed with this
software, and BlockyDevs neither endorses nor has reviewed this project.

It also reads from the public Hedera mirror node and links to HashScan, both
operated by third parties and used here as unmodified public services.

viewer/index.html embeds two MIT-licensed cryptography libraries by Paul Miller,
so that it can verify attestation signatures offline without a build step:

    @noble/ed25519    v3.0.0  Copyright (c) Paul Miller (paulmillr.com)
                              https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-ed25519
    @noble/hashes     v2.2.0  Copyright (c) Paul Miller (paulmillr.com)
                              https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-hashes

Both are redistributed under the MIT License. Their import and export
statements were stripped and each package wrapped in its own closure so the
code runs as a classic script from a file:// URL; the cryptographic code
itself is unmodified. The vendored block is marked as such in the file.
